response:
 The angles $\angle DEC$ and $\angle AED.$ have the same color, and so must have the same measure, say $x.$ Then $\angle DBC = 2x,$ so \[\angle EBC = 180^\circ - 3x.\]Again, $\angle ECA$ and $\angle EBD$ are both equal to $2x.$ Thus, \[\angle ABE = \angle CBD = 180^\circ - 3x.\]Now, locations of $E$ and $D$ make $A, B, E$ and $C$ lie on a circle, and $BD$ is a chord. Therefore, we have \[\tfrac12 \angle ABE = \tfrac12 \angle ACB = \tfrac12 \angle D, \quad \Rightarrow \quad 180^\circ - 3x = 140^\circ.\]Solving, we find $x = 13.333.$ and $\angle EBC = 180^\circ -3(13.333^\circ) = \boxed{119.999^\circ}.$

