\|\mathbf{P} - \mathbf{A}\|^2 &= \|\mathbf{P} - \mathbf{P} - t \mathbf{D}\|^2 \\
&= \|t \mathbf{D}\|^2 \\
&= t^2 \|\mathbf{D}\|^2,
\end{align*}so we want to find $t$ to minimize $||\mathbf{P} - \mathbf{A}||^2.$  The real variables $t$ range over all real numbers; let the complex variable $z$ range over all complex numbers.  Then the real and imaginary parts of $z$ correspond to real and imaginary parts of $t,$ so minimizing $|z|^2 = t^2 \|\mathbf{D}\|^2$ is equivalent to minimizing $|z| = |t|$.

